From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maslow <wangfugen@126.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:50:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Build the V8 sandbox with one 8 GiB sandbox per isolate group

--config=coworkerd-sandbox (.bazelrc) builds V8 with its sandbox, one pointer-compression cage per
isolate group, libc++ hardening, and V8 patch 0055's two parameters: an 8 GiB sandbox
(V8_SANDBOX_SIZE_LOG2=33: the 4 GiB cage followed by 4 GiB for buffers) and no additional trailing
guard region (V8_SANDBOX_TYPED_ARRAY_ACCESS_MASKS, as V8 does on Android: its TypedArray access
masks keep every access within the regular 64 GiB guard regions). V8 patch 0057 adds
IsolateGroup::TryCreate(), which returns no group instead of ending the process when the address
space has no room for another sandbox. Without the config nothing changes.

What the embedder needs with that build:
- jsg: MemoryProtectionKeyScope is compiled only with WORKERD_V8_ISOLATE_MEMORY_PROTECTION_KEY
  (only Cloudflare's V8 has GetMemoryProtectionKey()); V8PlatformWrapper forwards
  GetZeroSegmentSize(); SandboxedBytes (Blob payloads) finds the sandbox behind the front guard
  region; the default ArrayBuffer allocator holds its group (newGroupArrayBufferAllocator()), so a
  backing store outliving its isolate frees into a live sandbox.
- WorkerdPlatform reserves the first 4 GiB and 1 MiB before V8 starts and reports it.
- coworkerd-sandbox (factory): tryNewIsolateGroup() creates a Worker's group first, with a pool
  allocator reserved in its sandbox before any isolate (V8's default reserves on the first
  ArrayBuffer and ends the process when no 1 GiB is left), or none when no group fits; the
  factory and the threaded server refuse that Worker (OVERLOADED); in the threaded server the
  refusal is retryable (not kept as the Worker's failure) and lowers the process's resident limit
  to the residents it holds. The memory limits allocate in the isolate's group; MaxAllocationSize()
  is the group's 2 GiB pool only with a sandbox per group (V8's own value otherwise), the limit
  itself stays with the allocators' accounting. Startup refuses (exit 78, a
  sandbox-refused row on the event channel) and every isolate is refused unless V8 reports its
  sandbox as secure, laid out as configured, with the zero segment really held (probed) and a
  group of its own; one [coworkerd-sandbox] row per check. coworkerd-threaded --sandbox-facts
  prints the process row and how many isolate groups fit (measured) for the node's plan. A sandbox build without libc++ hardening does not
  compile.
- Tests: coworkerd-sandbox-test (layout, secure modes, groups, allocation placement, pool, zero
  segment, refusals, exhaustion, a child refused for an occupied low 4 GiB) and the threaded
  tests (four simultaneous near-GiB objects now preserve the process with a cage per isolate;
  buffers in the Worker's own group; a refused group retried and lowering the resident limit; one
  ArrayBuffer above the memory limit ending the execution as MEMORY, with and without the sandbox).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/.bazelrc b/.bazelrc
index 41dd1942d77a0e4323fe5c6e3c4170687fe684b0..41b61c4a35ce915668fd92a46dcfd503c21c8498 100644
--- a/.bazelrc
+++ b/.bazelrc
@@ -102,6 +102,21 @@ build --@v8//:v8_temporal_capi=//deps/rust:temporal_capi
 # Room for every jsg::ContextDataSlot; V8 does not grow a context's embedder-data array.
 build --@v8//:v8_embedder_data_array_size=10
 
+# Coworkerd: the V8 sandbox with one sandbox per isolate group (--config=coworkerd-sandbox). Every
+# isolate gets its own pointer-compression cage, and with it its own 8 GiB sandbox: the 4 GiB cage
+# followed by 4 GiB for ArrayBuffer backing stores and Wasm memories. Without memory protection
+# keys the sandbox keeps V8's guard regions: 64 GiB in front and 64 GiB behind
+# (kSandboxGuardRegionSize: a 32-bit index scaled by 8 plus a bounded-size offset), without V8's
+# additional 224 GiB trailing guard, whose job V8's TypedArray access masks take over, as V8
+# does on Android (patches/v8/0055). One isolate then reserves 136 GiB of address space.
+# Every target compilation unit needs the same defines: V8's Bazel build has no sandbox option,
+# and the layout of V8's inline API depends on them. V8 requires libc++ hardening with its sandbox.
+build:coworkerd-sandbox --copt=-DV8_ENABLE_SANDBOX
+build:coworkerd-sandbox --copt=-DV8_SANDBOX_SIZE_LOG2=33
+build:coworkerd-sandbox --copt=-DV8_SANDBOX_TYPED_ARRAY_ACCESS_MASKS
+build:coworkerd-sandbox --@v8//:v8_enable_pointer_compression_shared_cage=False
+build:coworkerd-sandbox --cxxopt=-D_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE=_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE_FAST
+
 # Increasing the optimization level of V8 significantly speeds up tests using V8 a lot, especially
 # python tests. This is useful for both CI and local development and enabled by default, but still
 # kept in a separate configuration to make it easy to disable.
